    "//SpiritSickness": "Spirit sickness source (plan section 28; wave0-spirits.md section 3, W0-19): a spirit that Harsh Wilds itself called turns on you. One action per spirit, each gated on a clamped 0-1 marker stat hw_stat_<spirit>_spirit_angry_pending (+1 in the Summoning's 'Angry Spirit' collection, -1 on the angry card's Continue) for the angry event card (hw_event_<spirit>_spirit_angry, CardType 3) that stays up until the player presses Continue. NOT RequiredCardsOnBoard: GameManager.CardIsOnBoard answers an Event card with EncounteredEvents.Contains, a saved never-pruned history list, so that gate stays true forever after the first angry event and the roll replays every 96 ticks. Never Earth, Darkness or Fear (their anger is already a curse or a mark). Two StatChangeTrigger entries (AND): hw_switch_spiritsickness {1,1} and the spirit's pending marker {1,1} (an unresolved trigger stat fails closed). RepeatOptions 0 (Repeat), ActionCooldown 96 and OncePerTick: one roll a game day per spirit while its card waits, so a card left unanswered does not roll every tick. Roll: Nothing (weight HW_SPIRIT_NOTHING = 1) against Sick (weight 2, a card-less drop too), two in three; Sick adds HW_SPIRIT_PER_ANGER = 96 to hw_spiritsickness. Each ActionName.DefaultText is its save-state key: unique, never renamed after release. Every number is a TUNABLE PLACEHOLDER, session-inferred and unmeasured against play.",
